        ("What is the difference between .then(), .catch(), and .finally() on a Promise?", ".then() handles fulfillment (and optional rejection). .catch() handles rejections. .finally() runs cleanup logic regardless of fulfillment or rejection without receiving arguments.", "Easy", "Comparison", "fetch(url)\n  .then(res => res.json())\n  .catch(err => console.error(err))\n  .finally(() => setLoading(false));", "Does .finally() return a promise?"),
